WEBVTT

1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,903
Hardening must be verified.

2
00:00:01,903 --> 00:00:07,215
A network can look well controlled in documentation while reality has drifted.

3
00:00:07,215 --> 00:00:26,005
Logs, alerts, configuration review, firewall rule review, access review, vulnerability management, drift detection, availability monitoring, DNS monitoring, certificate monitoring, and periodic tabletop exercises all help teams understand whether controls still work.

4
00:00:26,005 --> 00:00:29,097
Monitoring turns assumptions into evidence.

5
00:00:29,097 --> 00:00:39,879
Logs and alerts should help teams detect unexpected exposure, suspicious administrative access, failed changes, policy drift, and operational degradation.

6
00:00:39,879 --> 00:00:52,088
Device logs can show authentication failures, configuration changes, routing instability, VPN anomalies, wireless issues, or firewall denies that indicate a broken dependency.

7
00:00:52,088 --> 00:00:59,779
Alerts should be meaningful enough that responders know what changed, what is affected, and who owns the next step.

8
00:00:59,779 --> 00:01:02,792
Reviews catch the slow accumulation of risk.

9
00:01:02,792 --> 00:01:06,439
Firewall rules that were temporary become permanent.

10
00:01:06,439 --> 00:01:09,768
Access control lists grow broader than intended.

11
00:01:09,768 --> 00:01:12,781
VPN groups gain users who no longer need them.

12
00:01:12,781 --> 00:01:15,397
DNS records point to retired services.

13
00:01:15,397 --> 00:01:17,855
Certificates approach expiration.

14
00:01:17,855 --> 00:01:25,863
Configuration drift detection and periodic review make these issues visible before they become incidents or outages.

15
00:01:25,863 --> 00:01:28,717
Continuous review improves the baseline.

16
00:01:28,717 --> 00:01:40,926
When an incident, outage, audit finding, or near miss occurs, ask what should change: inventory, segmentation, access control, logging, alerting, patch process, or change review.

17
00:01:40,926 --> 00:01:44,653
Validation is not about proving the network is perfect.

18
00:01:44,653 --> 00:01:52,502
It is about confirming controls still match current risk and learning enough to make the next hardening cycle better.
